# Normalize line endings in the repository and in every checkout.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) rewrites LF to CRLF
# on checkout. Biome then wants to reformat every touched file, so `pnpm lint`
# fails locally for reasons that have nothing to do with the code — and only on
# Windows, while CI on Linux stays green. Pinning eol=lf makes the working tree
# match the repository and makes the gate portable.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows scripts must keep CRLF: cmd.exe won't run a LF shebang.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Keep diffs quiet for files git should never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.sqlite binary
*.db binary
